---
Implement brickwall limiter for master bus.

Prevents clipping by catching peaks above threshold with
instant attack and configurable release. Typically last in
the master effects chain.

## Parameters
- ceiling: Maximum output level (-6 to 0 dB, default -0.3)
- release: Release time (10-500 ms, default 50)

## Implementation
- Lookahead buffer (1-5ms) for transparent limiting
- Instant attack (within lookahead window)
- Smooth gain release

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] EFFECT_LIMITER added to effect type enum
- [ ] Output never exceeds ceiling level
- [ ] Transparent on signals below threshold
- [ ] Minimal distortion on moderate limiting

## Test Plan
- [ ] Hot signal limited to ceiling
- [ ] Quiet signal passes unchanged
- [ ] No clicks at onset of limiting
